 #:seon.task{:name "file-backed-branch-without-republication"
             :plan "`seon.test-support/with-published-file-database` acquires a Datahike branch of the executing published source, carrying its projection and writing to a private Konserve file frontend. It must preserve real blob staging and independent fixture writes without calling `seon.test-support/populate-published-root!` or `seon.cluster/refresh-source!`. The tagged `seon.test-support-test/a-file-backed-fixture-costs-a-branch` measures complete acquisition, body and release with `seon.profile/measure`, including the remaining `datahike.store/ready-store` synchronization. The owner accepted :tiered with the range-enabled Konserve fork and bounds derived from measured acquisition; removing the file overlay's asynchronous empty-file read is a separate task. Evidence and parent/change costs live in fixture-hour.md. Read `seon.blob/stage-binary!`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/fixture-hour.md`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/round-waste.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/round-waste/evidence.edn`."}
