             :plan "`seon.test-support/assign-task!` returns nil whatever `seon.task/create!` and `seon.task/assign!` answer, so a refused assignment is silent. Given an agent's branch connection, it declares its proof on that branch while `seon.task/assign!` reads the proofs on the connection it is given (main), refuses :no-proofs, and the test continues unassigned (lane a1-home, 2026-10-08: the first draft of `seon.turn-work-test/a-branch-agent-assigned-after-its-fork-opens-its-model-turn` failed for this reason). Correct: the helper declares the proof where the task lives and fails the test on any refusal value. Done when a call that `seon.task/assign!` refuses fails loudly at the helper. Read `seon.test-support/declare-proof!`."}
