             :plan "Make `seon.background-blob-test/background-binary-results-remain-exact-across-the-inline-threshold` reach its byte assertions through the production effect entrance. The parent fixture lacks its agent's cluster. The retained repair seeds it, uses `seon.test-support/revision` instead of hand-authored declarations, and carries the projection state. `seon.effect/context-handler` then reports SCI analysis unable to resolve `invalid-utf8` while `seon.sci.kernel/ensure-function!` installs `seon.background-blob-test/binary-handler`. Find and repair that installation's producer; do not replace the handler or add a second evaluator. The attempted fixture changes are retained as a patch and were not accepted with the range-read fixture change. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/fixture-hour/tiered-batch/background-fixture-candidate.patch`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/fixture-hour/tiered-batch/parent-results.edn` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/fixture-hour/tiered-batch/reaching-results.edn`."}

 #:seon.task{:name "tests-read-the-evaluations-recorded-data-not-printed-text"
             :plan "Tests read a reply's items as the data the evaluation recorded, never by re-reading its printed text (CLAUDE.md \"Tests read reply items by content (the shared test-support reader)\"). Today `seon.test-support/reply` calls `read-string` on the printed MCP text, and commit 130526a8b added a catch of `RuntimeException` around that read so a cut value (`{:message \"abc\"…+3808}`) answers `{::cut … ::cause …}`: that catch is a fence (CLAUDE.md \"NO GUARDS OR FENCES\") standing in for the root cause, which is that the harness only receives the JSON string the MCP path prints. Root cause to fix: give the test harness the evaluation's recorded data (the eval request's in-process answer or its recorded evaluation entities and result handles), so `reply`, `mcp-reply` and the evaluation-item readers assert on data; delete the catch and the `::cut` shape in the same commit. Evidence: `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/storage-nodes-missing.md`. About 93 call sites reference `reply`/`mcp-reply`. Needs a design pass first (which data the harness can hold without a second eval path). Proof: `seon.test-support-test/a-cut-reply-is-answered-as-data` rewritten to assert the recorded data with no catch."}
